This study examines hadronic matrix elements for three-body leptonic $	au$ decays, which are essential for interpreting experimental data. We evaluate the matrix elements for $	au^- 	o \pi^- \pi^- e^-  ar{
u}_e$ and $	au^- 	o K^- K^- e^-  ar{
u}_e$ utilizing vector meson dominance and $ho$-$K^*$ dominance models, respectively. Furthermore, we analyze the process $	au^- 	o \pi^- \pi^- \pi^- e^-  ar{
u}_e$ by decomposing the four-body matrix element into four distinct three-body components, each treated with a specific vector meson dominance model.
